    {
      "name": "79ae5a2c",
      "displayName": "NYC Service Gap Dashboard",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "title",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "## NYC Rodent Service Gap — ZIP Code Story\n",
                "\n",
                "Each NYC ZIP code blends **311 rodent complaints** (what residents report) with **DOHMH restaurant inspections** (what inspectors verify). The **Restaurant Service Gap Index** compares inspector-verified rodent evidence to commercial-only 311 reporting density — a high index means inspectors find rodent problems that businesses aren't calling about. **Residential complaint volume is ranked separately** because it has no restaurant denominator. Select a ZIP code from the dropdown above to explore its story, including honest data-sufficiency caveats for low-volume areas like JFK Airport (11430)."
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 12,
            "height": 3
          }
        },
